[0.0, "o", "\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                        -- USER REQUEST --\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFix issues 1578 to 1582. Can we do all in one session using coder skill? Parallel BUILD? Or mutipl\n  e sessions?\n"]
[2.2, "o", "\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                        -- ORCHESTRATOR ANSWERS: FIVE PARALLEL SESSIONS --\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHere's the answer to your question, based on the skill and the five issues:\n**Short answer: five parallel sessions, one per issue ? not one session with parallel BUILD.**\n**Why not one session with parallel BUILD?**\n- The BUILD Sharding Protocol shards *one plan's* files/steps across worktrees, but CHECK runs exa\n  ctly once on the *merged whole diff* and PR creation produces a single PR. Five unrelated refact\n  ors merged into one PR would be one giant, mixed-scope PR ? harder to review, harder to revert, \n  and it conflicts with the repo's \"implement only the assigned issue\" rule.\n- Each session's handoff dir (`02-plan.json`, `03-build.json`) is shaped around one issue's plan; \n  the skill has no notion of five plans per session.\n**Why five sessions works well here:**\n- The five issues are genuinely independent and touch disjoint areas:\n  - #1578 `exec_command` output filtering (ShellOutput)\n  [...]\n"]
[4.4, "o", "\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                       -- PLAN APPROVED --\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nYes\nPlan validated. Spawning BUILD for 1582:\n"]
